-- title:
--   Transport of the node package along the level-field identification, q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 3$ (`hq3`) and $M'$ a nonzero level with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`).
--
--   **Arithmetic and moduli data.** A guard prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ (`hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`). A valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`, i.e. `A.LiesOverPrime q`). A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC … M'`), required by `hW` to be exactly `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the set of places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace`, together with a distinguished element $s \in W$. An inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` — the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field — into `fieldBar q M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'` (the kernel of a reduction map of unit groups). A constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ onto `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal, compatibility with constants, a degree-preserving map on places, and the divisor clauses of the structure `ConstantReduction`; the hypothesis `hR₀` demands that a Laurent series over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` and has $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction of that series.
--
--   **Ground field and base ring.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hπ`), and the valuation subring $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ (written as the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$), assumed to be a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), Henselian (`hhens`) and with algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); the hypothesis `hκ` requires that every element of $A$ be congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary parameters.** A prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$ (`hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'`); an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity (`hζ₀`); an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hϖtA`) with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`); an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ required to be trivial (`hKb`: $K_b = \bot$), a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$ (`hAb`), and a nonzero generator $\varpi_b$ of its maximal ideal (`hϖb`, `hϖb0`); a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi \in k_0$ (`hξ`); and the tameness hypothesis `htame`, that $\ell_g - 1$ is a unit of $A_0$.
--
--   **Level group, function field and chart.** The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ is required (`hH₁`) to be `levelH q M'` intersected with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. The field $K_\ell$ is an intermediate field of the Laurent series field over $k_0$, required (`hKℓ`) to equal `laurentBaseChange k₀ (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`, and $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ is nonzero with Laurent series the coefficientwise image of `jq` (`hjℓ`); further `hjK` places `jqNModC k₀ q` in $K_\ell$. Write $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A₀ Kℓ jℓ` for the $A_0$-subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$. An ideal $y$ of $C$ is assumed maximal (`hy`) and to contain the image of $\pi_0$ (`hϖy`). There are $\varpi_t' \in A_0$ with $\varpi_t' = \varpi_t$ (`hϖt'`) and $m \ge 1$ (`hm1`) with $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t'\cdot(\text{unit})$ (`hm`); an element $a_0 \in A_0$ with `hjC` placing `jqNModC k₀ q` in $C$ and `ha₀y` placing `jqNModC k₀ q` $- a_0$ in $y$.
--
--   **Conditions at $y$.** `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the image of `jChartFin` (that is, of $j_\ell$) lies in `ssJSet q Ω`, the set of $j$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion affine point. `hover`: for every rational $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change lies in `R₀.integers`, which has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` where `jq` does, whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, and whose image `coeffEmb k₀ g` lies in $K_\ell$ and in $C$: for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals the value $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of $g$ and $c$ lies in $y$. `hOrbit`: every maximal ideal $y'$ of $C$ containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying the same condition as in `hover` is obtained from $y$ by a level automorphism: there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` (the normalised $q$-expansion identity relating $\tau$ and the action of $\gamma^{-1}$ on modular forms for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$) which preserves $C$ and satisfies $f \in y \iff \tau f \in y'$.
--
--   **The rigid chart block `hS1`** (fourteen clauses, summarised here) concerns a subalgebra $B_t \subseteq K_\ell$ over $A_0$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ containing $B_t$ (`hBW`): $C \subseteq B_t$; $K_\ell$ is the fraction field of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$; $B_t/\pi_0$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $W_t \cap k_0 = A_0$; the maximal ideal of $W_t$ is generated by $\pi_0$ and $W_t$ is a discrete valuation ring; $y$ is the contraction to $C$ of the maximal ideal of $W_t$, and $W_t$ is the localisation of $B_t$ at that maximal ideal; for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A_0$ there is a surjection $\rho$ of $B_t$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) of that residue field, with kernel the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W_t$, compatible with constants, and equivariant for level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ through an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c \neq 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$, and with a further level automorphism realising the pair $(1,c)$; $B_t$ is stable under level automorphisms for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is carried onto the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W_t$ by some level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; and an element of $B_t$ sent into the maximal ideal of $W_t$ by all such level automorphisms is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   **Inertia and deck data.** A natural number $n$ with $1 \le n$ (`hn1`), $n \mid q+1$ (`hnq`) and $n = 2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$ (`hn`), where `placeWidthChar q M' s` is the quotient of `jWidthChar q` at the value of $s$ on `jGeomGen` by `placeRamificationJ M' s`; an element $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ (`hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`) and a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$ with `IsLevelAutAt … γ₀⁻¹ Kℓ τ₀` (`hτ₀`) preserving $W_t$ (`hτ₀W`); an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ with $\zeta_c^n = 1$ (`hζc`) and $\zeta_c^k - 1$ a unit for $0 < k < n$ (`hζcprim`).
--
--   **The ends block `hR7`** (twelve clauses, summarised here), for a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$: $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B_t$ pointwise while $\tau_0^k$ moves some element of $B_t$ for $0<k<n$; every level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with some $\tau_0^k$, $k<n$; `ends.card = q + 1`; level automorphisms with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ permute `ends`, and `ends` is a single orbit; $\tau_0$ preserves each end; distinct ends are separated by an element which is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; there is a finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra $B_c$, stable under the level automorphisms with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, contained in every end, with each end the localisation of $B_c$ at its units; a level automorphism mapping an end into $W_t$ preserves $W_t$; each end $O$ is a local Noetherian subring of $W_t$ containing $C$, with $O \cap k_0 = A_0$, with every element of $O$ congruent to a constant from $A_0$ modulo non-units, and with an isomorphism of the adic completion of $O$ onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion of $A_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^m$, matching a factorisation $c_xc_y = \pi_0^m u$, sending constants to `const`, $c_x$ and $c_y$ to unit multiples of `U` and `V`, with $c_y$ in and $c_x$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, with `jqNModC k₀ q` $- a_0$ going to a unit times $V^e$ for some $e \ge 1$, with $\tau_0$ inducing an automorphism $\theta_0$ which multiplies `U` by $\zeta_c$ and `V` by its inverse modulo the square of the maximal ideal, and together with a discrete valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_\ell$ and a subalgebra $B_x$ carrying the separation, Eisenstein-type (Igusa) and pole clauses stated there; finally, a dichotomy: a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with $k_0$-points $A_0$, containing $C$ and dominating $y$ either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the ends.
--
--   **The two separation hypotheses.** `hR9`: some $b \in B_t$ lies outside every valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ with $V \cap k_0 = A_0$, with $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal of $V$, and at which $j_\ell$ is non-integral in the sense that every monic polynomial over $A_0$ evaluated at $j_\ell$ is a unit of $V$. `hR10`: for every maximal ideal $y''$ of $C$ containing $\pi_0$ which is not the image of $y$ under any level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, there is $b \in B_t$ such that for all such $\gamma$, $\tau$, $b$ lies outside every valuation subring of $K_\ell$ containing $C$ and sending the $\tau^{-1}$-preimage of $y''$ into its maximal ideal.
--
--   **Naming block.** $G$ is the subgroup of $k_0$-automorphisms of $K_\ell$ generated by the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ (`hG`); $K_0$ is its fixed field (`hK₀`); $B_0$ consists of the $G$-invariant elements of $B_t$ (`hB₀`); $W_0'$ is the valuation subring of $K_0$ induced by $W_t$ (`hW₀'`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** With $k_0$ acting on `fieldBar q M'` through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ characterised by the property that $f \in F_0$ precisely when all Laurent coefficients of $f$ lie in $k_0$; for every $k_0$-algebra isomorphism $\varphi : K_0 \to F_0$ such that (i) for all $f \in K_0$ the coefficientwise base change along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the Laurent series of $f$ is the Laurent series of $\varphi f$; (ii) for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), every primitive $q$-th root of unity $\xi' \in k_0$ with $\zeta = \xi'$, every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ' q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ Kℓ τ`, $\tau$ preserves $K_0$ and $\varphi$ conjugates its restriction into `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; (iii) for every rational $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` with `coeffEmb k₀ g` in $K_\ell$ and in $K_0$, $\varphi$ sends it to the image of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of $g$ under `hle`; for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ which is the contraction of $W_0'$ along $\varphi^{-1}$; and for every subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` which is the image under $\varphi$ (followed by the inclusion of $F_0$) of the part of $B_0$ lying in $K_0$ — the following implication holds.
--
--   The antecedent is the node package over $K_0$: there exist a witness that the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of `jq` lies in `R₀.integers`, a witness that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, a witness of the Hasse relation $(\mathrm{res}_A a_0)^q = s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $K_0$ such that: (1) `nodes.card = q + 1`; (2) there is a subring $B_c$ of $K_0$, generated by the constants from $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set, contained in every node, with each node the localisation of $B_c$ at the elements which are units there; (3) every level automorphism attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ (for $\gamma^{-1}$, at $\xi$) carries each node into another node, in the sense that $f \in O \iff \tau f \in O'$ for $f$, $\tau f \in K_0$; (4) any two nodes are so related by some such $\gamma$, $\tau$; (5) distinct nodes are separated by an element which is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; (6) for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ with $k_0$-points exactly $k_0 \cap A$ and such that every $g$ as in `hover` (in `R₀.integers`, regular where `jq` is, with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$) lies in $K_0$ and in $V$ with difference from the matching constant in the maximal ideal of $V$: either all of $B_0$ lies in $K_0$ and in $V$, or $V$ dominates one of the nodes, all of whose non-units fall into the maximal ideal of $V$; (7) for each node $O$: $O \subseteq W_0'$, $O$ is local and Noetherian, $O \cap k_0 = k_0 \cap A$, every element of $O$ is congruent modulo non-units to a constant from $k_0 \cap A$, and there are $E_0 \ge 1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}v$ for some $v$ with $v, v^{-1} \in A$, a witness $\pi_0 \in O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ onto `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion of $A_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of that model, such that $c_xc_y = \pi_0^{E_0}u$; $\iota$ sends constants from $k_0 \cap A$ to `const`; $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U\,U$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V\,V$; $c_y$ lies in $W_0'$ and in its maximal ideal while $c_x$ does not; `jqNModC k₀ q` $- a_0$ lies in $K_0$ and in $O$ with $\iota$-image a unit times $V^e$ for some $e \ge 1$; there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_0$ containing $O$, with $k_0$-points $k_0\cap A$, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, carrying an element $t$ such that a polynomial over $k_0$ with $A$-integral coefficients taking a value in the maximal ideal at $t$ has all coefficients in that maximal ideal, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside its maximal ideal, such that every $g$ as above lies in $K_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ exactly when its $R_0$-residue vanishes, and, when that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $O$ with difference from the matching constant a non-unit of $O$; and such that every other node contains an element outside $W_x$; and finally there is a subring $B_x$ of $K_0$ contained in $B_0 \cap O$, whose elements have non-negative order at every place of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$ where $j_\ell$ does, with $O$ the localisation of $B_x$ at its units, with $K_0$ the field of fractions of $B_x$, with $B_x$ generated by the constants from $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set, and containing an element $b$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ with $k_0$-points $k_0 \cap A$, with $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal, at which `coeffEmb k₀ jq` (assumed to lie in $K_\ell$ and $K_0$) lies in $V$ and is non-integral in the monic-polynomial sense, and which fails to contain some element of $O$.
--
--   The consequent is the same package read on $F_0$: there exist a witness that the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of `jq` lies in `R₀.integers` with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, a witness `hJK` that `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` lies in `fieldBar q M'`, an element $a_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $(\mathrm{res}_A a_0)^q = s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ with: `nodes.card = q + 1`; a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$ generated by the constants from $k_0 \cap A$ and a finite set, contained in every node and with each node its localisation at units; for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` carries each node into another node (for elements of `fieldBar q M'` lying, with their image, in $F_0$); for every $\zeta$, any two nodes are so related by some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; distinct nodes are separated as above; the dichotomy for valuation subrings $V$ of $F_0$ with $k_0$-points $k_0 \cap A$ and the moduli clause phrased through the inclusion `hle` of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base changes of the functions $g$: either all of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $V$, or $V$ dominates one of the nodes; and for each node $O$: $O \subseteq W_0$, $O$ local and Noetherian, $O \cap k_0 = k_0 \cap A$, every element of $O$ congruent modulo non-units to a constant from $k_0 \cap A$, and the existence of $E_0 \ge 1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}v$ as above, of $\pi_0 \in O$, of $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with the same crossing model over the adic completion of $A_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$, satisfying $c_xc_y = \pi_0^{E_0}u$, the constants clause, $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U\,U$, $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V\,V$, $c_y$ in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal with $c_x$ outside it, the statement that `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` $-\,a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$ with $\iota$-image a unit times $V^e$ for some $e \ge 1$, the existence of a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ with all the clauses listed upstairs (containing $O$, $k_0$-points $k_0\cap A$, discrete with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, the separating element $t$ with its polynomial clause, $c_x$ inside and $c_y$ outside the maximal ideal, the moduli clause for the images under `hle` of the functions $g$ — membership in $W_x$, vanishing of the $R_0$-residue detected by the maximal ideal, and, when that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, membership in $O$ with non-unit difference from the matching constant — and an element of each other node outside $W_x$), and the existence of a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ contained in $B \cap O$, whose elements have non-negative order at every place of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ where the image of `jq` does, with $O$ the localisation of $B_x$ at its units, with $F_0$ the field of fractions of $B_x$, with $B_x$ generated by the constants from $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set, and containing an element $b$ outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ with $k_0$-points $k_0\cap A$, with $\pi_0$ in the maximal ideal, at which the image of `jq` lies in $V$ and is non-integral in the monic-polynomial sense, and which fails to contain some element of $O$.
--
--   This is the descent step which transfers the node data at a supersingular place — the $(q+1)$ branch rings, their crossing-model presentations, the moduli (Hasse) germ, the common chart, and the Igusa separation clauses — from the fixed field $K_0$ of the level group acting on the level-$q^2M'$ function field to the identified subfield $F_0$ of the level-$q$ field, in the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ frame at $q = 3$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd) in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve at $q$.
